2. Overall page composition










The page uses a dark agricultural visual identity.

The entire background is a very dark green photographic texture featuring large, overlapping tropical leaves.

The foliage is intentionally subdued. It is not supposed to compete with the information panels.

The composition is:
HEADER / BREADCRUMB
CROP INFORMATION HERO

Photograph · Crop identity · Planting data · Crop health

Growing Conditions

Weather · Temperature · Forecast · Chart


Water & Irrigation

Demand · Rainfall · Irrigation · Moisture



Soil & Crop Information

Soil photograph and measurements


Today's Tasks

Action list and button


Risks & Alerts

Two alerts

Crop Rotation






The overall composition is asymmetrical but carefully balanced.

The upper hero establishes the crop identity. The middle row presents live environmental conditions. The lower row presents soil data, recommended work, and potential problems.

3. Background and global styling
3.1 Background image
The background must cover the complete dashboard viewport.

Use a high-resolution dark green foliage photograph with:
- Large, glossy tropical leaves.
- Deep emerald shadows.
- Natural green highlights.
- Slightly blurred distant vegetation.
- No bright sky or prominent subjects.
- A dark overall exposure.
The background should use:
.dashboard {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow: hidden;

    background:
        linear-gradient(
            90deg,
            rgba(0, 18, 11, .90),
            rgba(0, 24, 14, .77),
            rgba(0, 17, 10, .91)
        ),
        url("/assets/forest-background.jpg")
        center center / cover no-repeat;
}


The photographic background is visible most clearly in the spaces between the cards and along the upper portion of the page.
