3.3 Card appearance
Every major card has the same fundamental visual treatment:
- Dark translucent green surface.
- Thin green border.
- Rounded corners.
- Slightly brighter internal top edge.
- Subtle green ambient glow.
- No hard black drop shadow.
- No solid white surfaces.
.panel {
    position: relative;

    background:
        linear-gradient(
            135deg,
            rgba(7, 58, 38, .94),
            rgba(2, 31, 21, .96)
        );

    border: 1px solid var(--border-green);
    border-radius: 19px;

    box-shadow:
        inset 0 1px 1px rgba(190, 255, 215, .08),
        0 5px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, .17);
}


The border should be visible but understated.

The brighter emerald borders are especially noticeable on the Water & Irrigation panel.
3.4 Global typography
Use Inter throughout.
font-family: "Inter", sans-serif;


The interface uses a compact, modern sans-serif type system.
- Headings: semibold or bold.
- Main crop name: bold.
- Numerical measurements: semibold or bold.
- Descriptions: regular.
- Supporting labels: regular.
- Status labels: semibold.
The screenshot uses relatively small supporting text because the information density is high.

