20. Responsive behavior
The uploaded image is the desktop reference. The desktop composition should take priority over mobile rearrangement.

At the reference width, maintain:
- Full-width hero.
- Two-card middle row.
- Three-column bottom region.
- Stacked alerts and rotation cards.
At smaller screen widths, use the following changes:
Viewport	Behavior
1200 px and above	Original three-region desktop composition
900–1199 px	Reduce hero and internal column widths
768–899 px	Stack some bottom columns
600–767 px	Stack middle cards
Below 600 px	Single-column mobile dashboard

The hero should transition from a horizontal layout into a vertically stacked layout on mobile.

The weather forecast should move below the temperature chart rather than overlap it.

The gauge should remain centered in its own metric region.

Do not simply scale the entire desktop screenshot down to fit mobile.
